- Updated approach_1 -> tries to solve it using ARIMA because RSI returned strong autocorrelation in Ljung. Failed. Tried ARIMA on Streak Duration. Though it failed Ljung, showed a small statistical edge where it can guess direction of streak duration 71% of the time in test data. Predictive edge, but not profitable strategy.
- Updated approach_2 -> Changed from GBC to LASSO (linear models might perform better in smaller sample data). Results show that most variables performed worse than random variable (Only exception: RSI_SMA_dist and OFI_Alignment/OFI_agg). It seems the only variable that isn't noise is RSI_SMA_dist